{
  "schema": "helm.gateway.conformance.scenario.v1",
  "id": "GW-024",
  "title": "A step-up proof admits a high-risk, irreversible or helm.authority.* approval, and any other proof leaves the attempt ESCALATED with both tokens unspent",
  "rule": {
    "statement": "An approval of a high-risk, irreversible or helm.authority.* effect is admitted only with a step-up proof: a token of scope helm.gateway.stepup, of the decide token's approver and tenant, whose one helm_step_up entry names the attempt, the approval digest shown (lower-case hex) and the method webauthn, and states user_verified true. With none, or with a proof of another scope, attempt, digest, method, approver or tenant, or one that does not state user verification, the approval is permission_denied (STEP_UP_REQUIRED), the attempt stays ESCALATED and neither the decide token nor the proof is used up, so the same decide token approves once a proper proof comes. A proof's jti is single-use across attempts. A proof presented for an effect that needs none, valid or not, is ignored.",
    "cites": [
      {
        "doc": "docs/architecture/gateway-effect-api.md",
        "section": "Step-up proof"
      },
      {
        "doc": "protocols/proto/helm/gateway/v1/gateway.proto",
        "section": "string step_up_proof = 4;"
      },
      {
        "doc": "protocols/proto/helm/gateway/v1/gateway.proto",
        "section": "[reason_code: STEP_UP_REQUIRED]"
      }
    ]
  },
